  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 142 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nStrong upper level ridging will continue into next week allowing for \ndry conditions to persist. As high pressure settles over the region, \nwarm air advection will continue to push milder air into the region. \nTemperatures will remain near or slightly above normals in the upper \n50s to low 60s, potentially even into the mid to upper 60s through \nmuch of next week. The exception will Wednesday and Thursday as weak \ntroughing digs south just to the east of Nebraska. This will allow \nfor some cooler air behind the trough dropping highs on both days \nacross north central Nebraska into the low to mid 50s. Elsewhere \nhighs will remain in the low to mid 60s. Overnight lows will also \nremain fairly mild in the mid to upper 30s through the week and even \nrising into the low 40s on Tuesday night. Again these lows will be \nwell above normals (normal in the mid to upper 20s).",
